==============================================================================
  DEMO D2: Real fix (key AND signature derived from the seed); thief searches 20,000 seeds
==============================================================================
  Search time              : 2.1s (9,680 seeds/s)
  Best BER the thief found : 0.250   (mean 0.500)
  Forgeries accepted       : 0/20,000  at threshold BER <= 0.125
  Theory, per try          : P[Bin(64,0.5) <= 8] = 2.78e-10  -> expected 5.56e-06 hits
  Work factor              : ~2^31.7 seeds (~2.5e+09 for a 50% chance)
                             = ~72 single-core hours at this rate:
                             feasible on a GPU or cluster. Hence timestamps still matter,
                             and RQ1 must set signature length T and threshold theta.
  Target level (T=256 bits, as in Uchida; same theta=1/8): ~2^120 per try

